# 002-tilegrid/rclk_dsp_intf_clkbuf/top.py spins forever on the XCK26.
#
# gen_sites() picked its two BUFCE_ROW drivers in the wrong order, in unbounded
# loops:
#
#     while left_bufce_out is None:      x -= 1   # nearest on the left, [0]
#     while right_bufce_out is None:     x += 1   # one on the SAME hdistr
#
# Neither loop has a bound, so if no BUFCE_ROW to the right drives the HDISTR
# that the nearest left one happens to use, x runs away and the process spins
# at 100% CPU forever, having written nothing. It is not a slow fuzzer: top.v
# stays 0 bytes indefinitely, and with make -j4 you get four of them.
#
# On the XCK26 this is every one of the four RCLK_DSP_INTF_CLKBUF_L tiles. The
# nearest left driver is on HDISTR 23; only 0, 1, 6, 11, 17, 20 and 22 exist to
# the right. A valid pair exists for all seven of those, so the search simply
# committed to the left driver before checking the right could match it.
#
# Fixed by collecting what the right side can match FIRST, then taking the
# nearest left driver whose HDISTR is among them, and by bounding every walk at
# the grid edge with an assert that names the tile and both sets. The two
# BUFCE_LEAF searches were unbounded in the same way and are bounded too.
#
# Verified: 2.1 s, and all four tiles get a pair.
--- a/fuzzers/002-tilegrid/rclk_dsp_intf_clkbuf/top.py
+++ prjuray/fuzzers/002-tilegrid/rclk_dsp_intf_clkbuf/top.py
@@ -88,6 +88,8 @@
 
