+        # Pick the left and right BUFCE_ROW drivers TOGETHER.
+        #
+        # This used to walk left for the nearest BUFCE_ROW, take its first
+        # entry, and only then walk right for one on the same HDISTR - in
+        # unbounded `while ... is None: x += 1` loops. If no BUFCE_ROW to the
+        # right happened to drive that HDISTR, x ran away and the fuzzer spun
+        # forever at 100% CPU, having written nothing. On the XCK26 that is
+        # every one of the four RCLK_DSP_INTF_CLKBUF_L tiles: the nearest left
+        # driver is on HDISTR 23, and only 0, 1, 6, 11, 17, 20 and 22 exist to
+        # the right. A valid pair does exist for all seven of those, so the
+        # choice was simply made in the wrong order.
+        #
+        # So: collect what the right side can match first, then take the
+        # nearest left driver whose HDISTR is among them.
         x, y = loc
